body:
After grading, exam.html shows score immediately with no animation. For Kai (ADHD), a brief animated reveal creates a moment of suspense that makes the score feel earned.

Spec: Score counter animation on exam.html grade reveal.

Behavior:
1. After gradeExam() runs, show score section
2. Count up from 0 to final % in ~600ms using requestAnimationFrame
3. On reach: flash green (if passing, score >= 80%) or show static (if not)
4. Max 1 sound hook (optional): window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('mcm:scoreReveal', { detail: { pct } })) — Kai can wire audio later

Implementation:
function animateScore(targetPct, el, duration) {
  var start = performance.now();
  function step(now) {
    var t = Math.min((now - start) / duration, 1);
    el.textContent = Math.round(t * targetPct) + '%';
    if (t < 1) requestAnimationFrame(step);
    else el.textContent = targetPct + '%';
  }
  requestAnimationFrame(step);
}

ADHD rules:
- Duration: 600ms max. No longer. Attention drops.
- No looping, no repeat. One reveal, done.
- If score >= 93%: add class 'grade-a-flash' which pulses green once (CSS keyframe, 300ms)
- Keep it snappy. Celebrate the result, not the wait.

